WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.462
Step five is query rewriting.

00:00:02.462 --> 00:00:07.937
The rewrite should improve search language without changing the user's intent.

00:00:07.937 --> 00:00:12.602
For example, a user may ask, can I send it back?

00:00:12.602 --> 00:00:19.083
A better search query could be return eligibility deadline after delivery refund policy.

00:00:19.624 --> 00:00:26.026
That adds vocabulary that may exist in policy documents, but it does not invent an answer.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:31.351
A bad rewrite would say, customer qualifies for a refund.

00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:34.116
That is no longer a search query.

00:00:34.116 --> 00:00:38.489
It has turned an uncertain question into an unsupported conclusion.

00:00:39.493 --> 00:00:41.855
Keep the original question in state.

00:00:41.855 --> 00:00:44.675
Store the rewritten query separately.

00:00:44.675 --> 00:00:51.050
The original question controls the final task; the rewritten query only helps retrieval.
